# Honored by `gcloud builds submit` when uploading the source tarball. Without
# this, .gitignore is used — but .gitignore doesn't cover JS build artefacts,
# so the upload bloats with node_modules.
#
# This list runs BEFORE .dockerignore: what it lets through is already uploaded
# by the time Docker starts filtering the context. So the local-only payloads
# that .dockerignore keeps out of the image are named here too, or a manual
# `gcloud builds submit` from the author's checkout ships them anyway. The
# triggers do not go through this path (they build from the GitHub commit), and
# that is precisely why the manual route is the one that goes unnoticed.
#
# Syntax note, in case this file and .dockerignore ever look inconsistent: this
# one is gitignore-shaped, where a bare name matches at ANY depth — which is why
# `node_modules` here needs no `**/` while its twin in .dockerignore does.

.git
.gitignore
.idea
.vscode
.serena
.claude

# Python
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache

# JS
node_modules
dist
build

# Secrets. `.env*` rather than the three names that happen to exist today: the
# root .env holds DATABASE_URL and ADMIN_TOKEN, app/.env holds
# VITE_ADMIN_TOKEN, and a variant nobody thought of (.env.staging) is exactly
# how the next one reaches a build tarball. Same rule in .dockerignore and
# app/.dockerignore, so context and upload agree.
.env*

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Local-only payloads, none of them copied by api/Dockerfile and every one of
# them gitignored — so a CI clone has none and only an upload from the author's
# checkout carries them. Mirrors the block in .dockerignore.
tools/inksight/weights
tools/inksight/out
data/corpora
data/derived/from-nc-sa
data/samples/own-hand
data/humanbench
tools/glyphbench/fixtures
tools/glyphbench/runs
tools/wordbench/fixtures
tools/wordbench/runs
runs
temp

# Repo-local artefacts we never want in the image
docs
tests
.github
MEMORY.md
